---
description: Keep every user-interface header visually centered across the application
alwaysApply: true
---

# Centered UI Headers

- Center all visible header and title text throughout the application.
- This includes page, section, card, modal, drawer, panel, table, and form headers.
- Centering must remain visually exact in RTL layouts even when actions or icons exist on either side.
- Use a balanced layout such as a three-column grid so side controls do not shift the title away from the true center.
- Preserve centered headers on mobile, tablet, desktop, print, and PDF views.
- Do not apply this rule to body copy, form labels, table cells, or ordinary content unless the design explicitly requires it.
- Any new or modified screen must be checked at mobile and desktop widths for true header centering.
